Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: ima: Downgrade error to warning

BugLink: http://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/1656908

Signed-off-by: Tim Gardner <tim.gardner@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00026
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@96afdb1618a1886331ee664a6a61456874a11d32
---
 security/integrity/ima/ima_fs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/security/integrity/ima/ima_fs.c b/security/integrity/ima/ima_fs.c
index 2a0bca554316..427c53279b72 100644
--- a/security/integrity/ima/ima_fs.c
+++ b/security/integrity/ima/ima_fs.c
@@ -541,7 +541,7 @@ static ssize_t ima_read_policy(char *path)
 	rc = kernel_read_file_from_path(path, 0, &data, INT_MAX, NULL,
 					READING_POLICY);
 	if (rc < 0) {
-		pr_err("Unable to open file: %s (%d)", path, rc);
+		pr_warn("Unable to open file: %s (%d)", path, rc);
 		return rc;
 	}
 	size = rc;
